# Movie Dubbing AI

A professional starter project for Bangla movie dubbing using open-source AI components.

This repository is built for local, Colab, and cloud testing workflows. It combines:
- Demucs for source separation
- pyannote for speaker diarization
- Whisper for transcription
- Ollama for Bangla script and emotion adaptation
- Coqui TTS / XTTS for voice synthesis
- lip-sync pipeline scaffolding for final dubbing output
- Streamlit UI for easy usage

The project is designed as a realistic open-source dubbing pipeline foundation for Bangla voice conversion and cinematic localization.

## Included stack

- Speech separation: Demucs
- Speaker diarization: pyannote.audio
- Transcription: Whisper
- Translation / script adaptation: Ollama + local LLM
- Voice synthesis: Coqui TTS / XTTS
- Final alignment: Wav2Lip / lip-sync workflow
- App UI: Streamlit

## Open-source models and libraries used

Recommended Hugging Face / open-source integrations:
- `suno/bark` (creative voice experiment)
- `coqui/XTTS-v2` (voice cloning)
- `openai/whisper` (ASR)
- `pyannote/speaker-diarization`
- `facebook/demucs` / `htdemucs` variants
- community Bangla fine-tuned TTS models (to be evaluated)
- Wav2Lip / Synctalk / SadTalker style lip-sync pipelines

