## Quick start

### 1) Clone

```bash
git clone https://github.com/atik4595-call/movie-dubbing-ai.git
cd movie-dubbing-ai
```

### 2) Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -U pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3) Run the app

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

### 4) Upload files in the UI

- Source video
- Reference voice
- Emotion (optional)
- Language: Bangla

## Ollama setup (recommended)

Install and run Ollama locally:

```bash
curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh
ollama pull llama3.1
```

Then use the script adaptation step for Bangla dubbing text and emotion tags.

## Colab note

This project is designed to be Colab-friendly. The repository includes a setup flow for GPU runtime and package installation, but actual model quality depends on:
- GPU availability
- package compatibility
- model download speed
- dataset quality
- Bangla voice fine-tuning quality

## Professional dubbing pipeline (what this repo attempts)

1. Extract audio from source video
2. Separate vocals/noise using Demucs
3. Identify speaker segments with pyannote
4. Transcribe using Whisper
5. Rewrite the dialogue in Bangla with emotion-aware wording using Ollama
6. Generate or adapt voice using TTS / XTTS / voice-cloning models
7. Estimate timing and align voices for lip-sync
8. Produce final dub-ready video output

## Important reality check

This repository is a professional starter framework, not a magically finished movie-dubbing product.
For best Bangla cinematic quality, you still need:
- a clean Bangla voice dataset
- fine-tuned TTS on your target voice
- controlled emotion styling
- a lip-sync model tuned for the target source face
- a real validation workflow for output quality

